# Conventional Commits

When creating git commits (only when the user asks), follow [Conventional Commits 1.0.0](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/).

## Format

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

- Type + optional scope + optional `!` + `: ` + short description (imperative, lowercase start, no trailing period)
- Body optional; blank line after description
- Footers optional; blank line after body
- Breaking change: `!` after type/scope, and/or footer `BREAKING CHANGE: ...`

## Types (use these)

| Type | When |
|------|------|
| `feat` | New user-facing capability |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `docs` | Docs only |
| `refactor` | Code change, no behavior change |
| `test` | Tests only |
| `chore` | Tooling, deps, misc maintenance |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `ci` | CI config |
| `build` | Build system / packaging |

Scope optional, e.g. `fix(parser):`, `feat(core-api):`.

## Examples

```
fix(message-handler): avoid crash when getChat returns null

feat(core-api): truncate package description to Core @Size limits

docs: document AI fallback hard-message fixtures

fix!: require webVersion pin for WhatsApp Store injection

BREAKING CHANGE: unpinned WA Web HTML is no longer supported locally.
```

## Do not

- Vague subjects: `update`, `fix stuff`, `wip`
- Past tense: `fixed` → use `fix: ...`
- Bundle unrelated changes; prefer focused commits when the user asks to split
